{{figure:fig_2_1.webp}}

The graph of the function $\text{f}$ is a straight line segment from $(0, 0)$ to $(2, 1)$.

Show that $\text{f}$ could be a probability density function.

{{figure:fig_2_2.webp}}

The graph of the function $\text{g}$ is a semicircle, centre $(0, 0)$, entirely above the $x$-axis.

Given that $\text{g}$ is a probability density function, find the radius of the semicircle.
